#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175808 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of an Object"}] :question/id #uuid "696213fa-757d-5450-906a-ffb0638599e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-9704" :question/problem "At full speed, a fully grown cheetah can cover a distance of $998$ feet in $10$ seconds. What is the speed of the cheetah when running at full speed?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in feet per second, we divide the number of feet, $998$, by the number of seconds, $10$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{998}{10} &= 99.8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the cheetah is $99.8$ feet per second."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175809 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time"}] :question/id #uuid "1c7eac8b-b163-532f-84f0-10ffd23a67f6" :question/math-academy-id "e-9705" :question/problem "Moving at a constant rate, it takes $8$ seconds for a particular type of fish to swim a distance of $200$ centimeters. Find the distance this fish can cover in $3$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in centimeters per second, we divide the number of centimeters, $200$, by the number of seconds, $8$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{200}{8} &= 200 \\div 8 \\\\\n&= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the fish is $25$ centimeters per second.\n\nTo find the distance covered in $3$ seconds, we multiply the speed by $3$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndistance &= speed \\cdot time \\\\\n&= 25 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 75\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fish can cover $75$ centimeters in $3$ seconds."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175810 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Time Given Distance and Speed"}] :question/id #uuid "cb7d1f42-a5bc-5fba-834c-07a2ceb0644a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9706" :question/problem "It takes $5$ days for the Earth to travel $13$ million kilometers around the Sun. How much time does it take for the Earth to travel $52$ million kilometers around the Sun?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in millions of kilometers per day, we divide the number of million kilometers, $13$, by the number of days, $5$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{13}{5} &= 13 \\div 5 \\\\\n&= 2.6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the Earth is $2.6$ million kilometers per day.\n\nTo find the time it takes the Earth to cover $52$ million kilometers, we divide the distance by $2.6$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ntime &= \\frac{distance}{speed} \\\\\n&= \\frac{52}{2.6} \\\\\n&= \\frac{52 \\cdot 10}{2.6 \\cdot 10} \\\\\n&= \\frac{520}{26} \\\\\n&= 520 \\div 26 \\\\\n&= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the Earth $20$ days to travel $52$ million kilometers around the Sun."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab2d3de-e0a5-5a0b-8420-dcdaa1076d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$165$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 175921861741